<?xml version="1.0"?>
<recovery>
    <pages>
        <page name="cyberfox">
            <template name="base_nav"/>
            <text style="text_ab_title">
                <placement x="%col1_x_indent%" y="%ab_bc_y%"/>
                <text>CYBERFOX // RECOVERY GUIDE</text>
            </text>
            <text style="text_body2_hl">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row0_a_y%"/>
                <text>BLUEJAY • PIXEL 6A • DIAGNOSTIC CONSOLE</text>
            </text>

            <text style="text_body1_hl">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row1_1a_y%"/>
                <text>INSTALL — Flash a compatible ROM, kernel, module, or recovery ZIP.</text>
            </text>
            <text style="text_body2">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row1_2a_y%"/>
                <text>Verify the package source, device support, Android base, and checksum before flashing. A ZIP can write partitions or erase data.</text>
            </text>

            <text style="text_body1_hl">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row2_1a_y%"/>
                <text>WIPE — Clear selected filesystems or user data.</text>
            </text>
            <text style="text_body2">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row2_2a_y%"/>
                <text>Cache and Dalvik cleanup is not a universal bootloop fix. Format Data erases internal user storage, including photos and downloads.</text>
            </text>

            <text style="text_body1_hl">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row3_1a_y%"/>
                <text>BACKUP / RESTORE — Save and recover supported partitions.</text>
            </text>
            <text style="text_body2">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row3_2a_y%"/>
                <text>Back up before changing ROMs or boot images. Copy backups off-device before formatting data.</text>
            </text>

            <text style="text_body1_hl">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row4_1a_y%"/>
                <text>MOUNT / PARTITIONS — Inspect storage and filesystem state.</text>
            </text>
            <text style="text_body2">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row4_2a_y%"/>
                <text>Mounting exposes a filesystem; it does not repair it. Do not format or resize partitions unless the device-specific instructions require it.</text>
            </text>

            <text style="text_body1_hl">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row5_1a_y%"/>
                <text>ADB / TERMINAL / LOGS — Diagnose before attempting repairs.</text>
            </text>
            <text style="text_body2">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row5_2a_y%"/>
                <text>Collect recovery.log, dmesg, slot state, and installer output. Logs help distinguish a bad module, incompatible kernel, encryption issue, or damaged image.</text>
            </text>

            <text style="text_body1_hl">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row6_1a_y%"/>
                <text>PIXEL 6A SAFETY — Recovery belongs to vendor_boot on Tensor devices.</text>
            </text>
            <text style="text_body2">
                <placement x="%gl_text_x%" y="%row6_2a_y%"/>
                <text>Never flash a boot.img, init_boot.img, vendor_boot.img, or vbmeta.img from another build or device. Confirm the active slot and image provenance first.</text>
            </text>

            <button style="btn_raised">
                <placement x="%btn_raised_left_x%" y="%row_btn7_y%"/>
                <text>ADVANCED TOOLS</text>
                <action function="page">advanced</action>
            </button>
            <button style="btn_raised_hl">
                <placement x="%btn_raised_right_x%" y="%row_btn7_y%" placement="1"/>
                <text>BACK TO FILES</text>
                <action function="page">filemanagerlist</action>
            </button>
            <template name="gestures"/>
            <action>
                <touch key="back"/>
                <action function="page">advanced</action>
            </action>
        </page>
    </pages>
</recovery>
